# Prompt Log — Integrating Crossy Road into Personal Website

## 1. Task Overview

**Task:** Integrate a browser-based Crossy Road game into an existing personal portfolio website.

**Website:**  
https://david555787.github.io/jessielu.github.io/

**Goal:**  
Add the Crossy Road game as a project within the personal website so that users can click the “Crossy Road” project and be redirected to a playable version of the game.

---

## 2. User Request

The user wanted to add a newly created web game to their personal website. The game consisted of three files:

- `index.html`
- `style.css`
- `script.js`

The user specifically requested that the existing **Crossy Road** project on the portfolio become clickable and redirect visitors to the playable game.

---

## 3. Files Provided

The following files were provided for the game:

### `index.html`
Contains the structure of the Crossy Road game, including:

- Game canvas
- Score display
- Best score display
- Start screen
- Game-over screen
- Control instructions
- Start and restart buttons

The HTML file links to:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
<script src="script.js"></script>
```

### `style.css`
Controls the appearance of the game, including:

- Game layout
- Canvas styling
- HUD
- Start and game-over overlays
- Buttons
- Typography
- Colors and visual effects

### `script.js`
Contains the main game logic, including:

- Player movement
- Keyboard controls
- Touch/swipe controls
- Vehicles
- Logs
- Trains
- Collision detection
- Score tracking
- Procedurally generated lanes
- Game rendering using HTML Canvas

